{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2UKh5nh3ogU78HDLjn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `cachelib/lru.py` to the spec and added 16 tests in `tests/test_lru.py`. All 16 pass (`python3 -m pytest -q tests`).\n\nThe cache uses an `OrderedDict` of `key -> (value, expires_at)`, so every operation is O(1) on average. I also added an empty `tests/__init__.py` so the tests import `cachelib` cleanly. Nothing is committed.\n\nChoices I made where the spec was silent:\n\n- **TTL is measured from the last `put`.** A `get` refreshes recency but does not extend the TTL.\n- **`__contains__` does not touch recency or the hit/miss counters.** It does remove an expired entry it finds and counts that as an expiration.\n- **`__len__` counts stored entries, including expired ones not yet removed.** Expired entries are removed lazily on `get` or `in`. Excluding them would need an O(n) sweep, which breaks the O(1) requirement. If you want `len` to exclude expired entries, tell me and I'll change it.\n- **Putting into a full cache with expired entries still evicts the LRU entry.** It does not sweep expired entries first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5945,"cache_read_input_tokens":37766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5945},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e256d482-77fa-4328-a8fe-119fc2fb286c","uuid":"9a3d673e-bd19-4014-9327-08113ff18682","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:04:27.634Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs2UKSTG5ew53aFaQVRG"}
